@lisongqian Thanks for the suggestion. I have opened Discussion #969 to describe the longer-term direction for per-sandbox observability, the current PoC architecture, and possible integration paths. The Discussion also clarifies that the initial observability PoC will use vsock as the baseline. `ivshmem` remains a possible optimization for high-volume event delivery if later measurements show a meaningful benefit.

For this PR, could you help review whether the current template-level opt-in ivshmem implementation is suitable as an experimental communication primitive, including its implementation quality and runtime behavior? If the implementation and validation are acceptable, would it make sense to merge it first? Consumer-specific protocols, control components, synchronization, and flow-control mechanisms could then be introduced separately by follow-up integrations that need them.

If additional validation or a minimum end-to-end scenario is required before merging, please let me know which cases you would like covered.

